  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "RTD folds ASCII case on ProgID, matches topics case-sensitively after CONCAT coercion, and returns #N/A with no server",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, RTD(progid, server, topic1, ...) requires a ProgID, server, and 1 to 253 topic arguments; returns the first error argument in argument order before looking up any server; folds ASCII case on progid while comparing topic strings case-sensitively and space-sensitively after CONCAT-style text coercion (so 1 and \"1\", TRUE and \"TRUE\", and 0.1+0.2 and \"0.3\" share one topic); returns #N/A when no COM RTD server exists for progid; and shows 0 for an empty RTD reply.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527 across 120/120 pinned rows (RTD.json), 1,546/1,546 full-bank rows, and dc-snz.23.4 topic-key probes (udf.rs).",
